# Constellation — root build context ignore (shared by both Dockerfiles).
# Keeps the context small AND prevents host-built artifacts / secrets from
# leaking into an image. node_modules in particular MUST be excluded: the
# host's pnpm store links are invalid inside Linux containers.

# dependencies
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# build output
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# turbo / tooling caches
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
**/coverage
.nyc_output

# vcs & CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# env & secrets — NEVER bake these into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# docker's own files (not needed inside the build)
docker-compose*.yml
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/.dockerignore
Makefile

# docs & editor noise
docs
*.md
!README.md
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# local data
data
tmp
*.log

# brain (Graphify) — the corpus and the graph are BIND/VOLUME mounts at
# runtime, never build inputs. graphify-out in particular can reach tens of
# MB (graph.json + graph.html) and would bloat every api/web build context.
graphify-out
**/graphify-out
brain
